      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "[Upbeat Indie Music Playing]\n\nHost: \"Hey friends, welcome to the first episode of 'The Real Truth.' Today we're tackling a new trend that's everyone's bedtime horror story - why is everything so expensive? Let's get right into it. You know, it's like watching two train tracks heading in different directions - the tracks for Big Government and Big Business, while the 'Free Market' side is a rusted cobweb of left-behind dreams and broken promises.\n\n\n\nNow don't get me wrong, this wasn't always like this. Back then, experts in Faraway Land would study paperwork and at dinner parties the pied pipers would say theories were based on fact, when in actuality, some plumbers were working rung jobs that support Uncle Sam himself.\n\n,\n\nBut they've got a new trick up their pants - they're more skilled in robot friends than lead bullets. No sweat. Bots ain't getting your plasma TV and pacifier, or your sweet little girl to the local No-Doubt-about-It Diner.\n\n,\n\nWith everyone being too busy to manhandle an IKEA flatpack, and the GPS satellites busy calming consumer panic, the economists' spreadsheets are winning again, as professional economists supply our political uber-madmen with dollar signs.\n\n,\n\nNever mind that old saying",
